comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T08:16:03.790Z",claude-code-agent,"Duplicate check: searched all statuses for npm prerelease explicit tag, release publish tag latest, and same-day release. No item records this exact npm dist-tag contract failure; pm-cedo0g tracks the parent Bun recovery incident and is linked rather than duplicated."
  "2026-07-24T08:17:24.701Z",claude-code-agent,"TDD evidence: the workflow contract first failed against the untagged npm publish command, reproducing the hosted run 30077790348 failure. After adding the explicit latest dist-tag, all 10 workflow contract tests pass; docs links and build also pass."
  "2026-07-24T08:21:04.328Z",claude-code-agent,"Pre-PR evidence: repo-wide static quality passed with 100% source, exported, and member docstring coverage; 354 files and 6,213 tests passed at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage (42,684 statements, 30,277 branches, 8,689 functions, 41,488 lines). Focused workflow contract, docs links, and build also pass."
  "2026-07-24T08:35:07.838Z",claude-code-agent,"Review remediation: CodeRabbit correctly identified that the negative contract only rejected the original exact untagged command. The assertion now rejects every npm publish line lacking --tag latest, including trailing-flag and duplicate-command variants. Focused 10-test workflow contract and repo-wide static quality pass."
  "2026-07-24T08:41:02.345Z",claude-code-agent,"Second review remediation: CodeRabbit verified the production publish path and identified an inline-shell bypass in the negative contract. The matcher now recognizes npm publish at shell command boundaries and includes an explicit inline if/then regression case. Focused workflow tests and static quality pass."
  "2026-07-24T08:51:44.409Z",claude-code-agent,"Review-loop evidence: CodeRabbit identified brace-group shell syntax as the final bypass of the release-workflow every-publish invariant. Exact-head fix expands the command-boundary matcher to include braces and adds a direct '{ npm publish --access public; }' regression assertion. Verification passed: 10/10 focused CI workflow contract tests and the complete repo-wide quality:static gate (100% docstring/export/member requirements, package boundary, and token-budget checks). The prior hosted smoke failure was independently rerun once; all packed-package, 88-command dogfood, MCP/plugin, runtime, coverage, typecheck, compatibility, and static jobs are green, confirming a transient session-start timeout."
  "2026-07-24T08:58:03.484Z",claude-code-agent,"Final prefix remediation: CodeRabbit's exact-head review confirmed stable-channel semantics and found Bash's logical-negation prefix as one remaining command-boundary form. The contract now rejects '! npm publish --access public' without --tag latest through an explicit regression assertion. Focused workflow contract remains 10/10 green and repo-wide quality:static passes in full."
  "2026-07-24T09:04:37.643Z",claude-code-agent,"Merge evidence: PR #670 merged to main at fa4c0441 after exact-head 4e9dfd125476ed6cdac6472c17b67414ca34b83a passed every hosted check. Review inventory had zero unresolved threads; all actionable CodeRabbit findings were fixed, reacted to, and answered. The final requested rerun was externally rate-limited, with no new code finding. This item closes for the merged workflow/contract fix; pm-cedo0g remains active for production release recovery."
